# Range Rover L405, 2012-2021.
#
# The fourth-generation Range Rover: 4,999 mm long, 1,984 mm body width (2,073
# with mirrors), 1,835 mm high, 2,922 mm wheelbase; all-aluminium body, 3.0 V6
# and 4.4 V8, long-wheelbase option from 2014. The most numerous modern luxury
# 4x4 in Britain: about 29,800 L405s licensed in 2019.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Range_Rover#Fourth_generation_(2012)
#
# Colours: Santorini Black, Loire Blue, Indus Silver and Corris Grey are period
# Range Rover finishes.
#
# Weight: 55 in total (black 18, silver 15, blue 12, grey 10), the largest class-4
# 4x4 parc of the 2010s.
#
# Speed 220 km/h; comfort 160/570 (line). Classes 3,4.
# Dates: 2012-2021 with a road tail to about 2028.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/range-rover-l405.blend. References:
# citycars/references/range-rover-l405/ (gitignored). Images via Wikimedia Commons.

obj=citycar
name=RangeRoverL405(SantoriniBlack)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=18
intro_year=2012
intro_month=9
retire_year=2028
retire_month=6
speed=220
class=3,4
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=160
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=570

